1) Camunda
    Camunda is a tool where you create workflows (using BPMN) and decision rules (using DMN), and it executes them by calling your code, APIs, and services.
                                                            or
    Camunda is an open‑source workflow and decision automation platform that helps you model, run, and automate business processes using BPMN, DMN, and CMMN standards.


2) Camunda Modeller
     A Tool that helps us in easily creating BPMs and DMNs.

3) BPMN
      BPMN is a business processing modelling notation
      - It is an open standard to diagram business process.
      Ex:-
                                 TASK 1                    Task2
                             ___________________        ________________
            start    O----> |    Insert user    |----->| Get all Users   | ---> O  END
                            |        to DB      |      |     DB          |    
                            ____________________       _________________
         * The framework that actually supports the BPM is called Camunda.
         * So, Camunda is a framework that is actually responsible for execution of the BPM files.


4) Process Enginer
        * A Process engine is the core component inside a BPM platform(like Camunda) that executes, manages and controls business processes defined using BPMN diagram.
        * A Java library that understands BPMNs and DMNs and is reponsible for executing them.

5) Ways to integrate a process engine in our application
        A Process ENgine can integrated into our application in 3 main ways :-
            1) Embedded Process Engine
                    * Process Engine is added as a library to a custom app.
            2) Shared, container - Managed Process Engine
                    * Process Engine is provided as a container service and can be shared by all applications deployed inside the container.
            3) Standalone (Remote) Process Enginer Server
                    * Process Engine is hosted on a standalone server.
                    * The application which could be hosted somewhere else can connect to remote process Engine.

6) Camunda Generic-properties
         Camunda Generic Properties are the basic configuration settings available for every BPMN element in Camunda Modeler.
       *  They are called “generic” because they apply to all types of BPMN elements, such as:
                Start Event
                End Event
                Service Task
                User Task
                Gateway
                Timer
                Message Event
                Subprocess
        These properties help you configure the identity and behavior of the element inside your workflow.
